WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.802
India has nuclear weapons,

2
00:00:01.802 --> 00:00:03.862
but hasn't signed the Non-Proliferation

3
00:00:03.862 --> 00:00:05.875
Treaty. Here's how that came

4
00:00:05.875 --> 00:00:06.826
about.

5
00:00:07.157 --> 00:00:09.366
India's first test was at

6
00:00:09.366 --> 00:00:10.932
Pokhran in 1974.

7
00:00:10.932 --> 00:00:13.475
Five more followed in May

8
00:00:13.475 --> 00:00:15.049
1998. In 2008,

9
00:00:15.049 --> 00:00:17.343
the Nuclear Suppliers Group gave

10
00:00:17.343 --> 00:00:19.120
India a waiver for civil

11
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.106
trade.

12
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.160
The doctrine of 2003: no

13
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:22.961
first use,

14
00:00:22.961 --> 00:00:25.317
and credible minimum deterrence.

15
00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:27.160
And no use against countries

16
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.211
without nuclear weapons.

17
00:00:29.551 --> 00:00:31.185
India sees the N-P-T as

18
00:00:31.185 --> 00:00:34.231
discriminatory. It freezes which countries

19
00:00:34.231 --> 00:00:35.858
may hold weapons.

20
00:00:36.547 --> 00:00:37.718
Your turn.

21
00:00:37.718 --> 00:00:40.071
What are the 1998 tests

22
00:00:40.071 --> 00:00:41.283
called?
